UNIT_ID: U-022
NAME: Sensecape — Multilevel Exploration and Sensemaking via Canvas and Hierarchy Views
LENS: LENS_ARTIFACT
TYPE: interface_contract
STATUS: SOURCE_SUPPORTED
FUNCTION: Interfejs do eksploracji i sensemaking z LLM przez externalization of levels of abstraction: canvas view (infinite whiteboard z nodes, expand bar, text extraction, semantic zoom, semantic dive) + hierarchy view (3D pseudo-space z canvases, broad topic, subtopics); users switch between foraging i sensemaking loops.
MINIMAL_FORM:
  - canvas view: node-first approach (double-click to add node); expand bar (Prompt, Explain, Questions, Subtopics); text extraction (highlight & drag to new node); semantic zoom (All → Summary → Keywords based on zoom level); semantic dive (double-click node to create new canvas layer below)
  - hierarchy view: overview of information space; add higher-level canvas (Broad Topic), lower-level canvases (shadow underneath); create new hierarchies, connect hierarchies via higher-level topic
  - LLM used for: summarizing canvas content into topic, generating Questions/Subtopics, recommending subtopics in hierarchy view
SOURCE_ANCHOR:
  - source: Sensecape: Enabling Multilevel Exploration and Sensemaking with Large Language Models
    locator: arXiv:2305.11483v2
    anchor: §3.2 User Interface & Features (Canvas View, Hierarchy View), §3.1 Motivating Scenario (C1–C6)
    revision: UNKNOWN
EVIDENCE_TYPE: SOURCE_FACT
EVIDENCE_LAYER: DOCUMENTED_DESIGN
EFFECT_STATUS: TESTED_IN_SOURCE
TRANSFER_FORM: INTERFACE
LIMITS:
  - user study: within-subject N=12; tasks: AI impact on work, global warming on economy; 20 min per task; Sensecape users explored more topics (M=10.8 vs 7.3), structured knowledge more hierarchically (M=4.3 vs 2.6 levels)

